Architecture: Encoder-Decoder (No Attention)

🧠 Goal: Translate

Input (English):

"The cat ate"  

Target (Spanish):

"El gato comió"


⸻

⚙️ Architecture: Encoder-Decoder (No Attention)

Parameters:
	•	Vocab size (English/Spanish): 6 words each
	•	Embedding dimension: 2
	•	LSTM units: 2
	•	Sequence length: 3

⸻

🔤 Step 1: Vocabulary & Tokenization

English Vocab:

Word	Token
the	1
cat	2
ate	3

Input sequence: [1, 2, 3] → “the cat ate”

Spanish Vocab:

Word	Token
	0
el	1
gato	2
comió	3
	4

Target Input: [0, 1, 2] → <START> el gato
Target Output: [1, 2, 3] → el gato comió

⸻

🔢 Step 2: Embedding Lookup

English Embedding Matrix (2D):

E_eng = {
  1: [0.1, 0.3],   # the
  2: [0.2, 0.6],   # cat
  3: [0.7, 0.9]    # ate
}

So input becomes:

X = [
  [0.1, 0.3],
  [0.2, 0.6],
  [0.7, 0.9]
]  # shape = (3, 2)


⸻

🧮 Step 3: Encoder LSTM (manually, 1 unit)

We simulate a simplified LSTM with:
	•	Weight Wx = [0.5, 0.1]
	•	Recurrent Wh = [0.4, 0.2]
	•	Bias b = 0

Start with:
	•	h₀ = 0

t=1 (word = “the”):

x₁ = [0.1, 0.3]
h₁ = tanh(0.5*0.1 + 0.1*0.3 + 0.4*h₀) = tanh(0.05 + 0.03 + 0) = tanh(0.08) ≈ 0.08

t=2 (word = “cat”):

x₂ = [0.2, 0.6]
h₂ = tanh(0.5*0.2 + 0.1*0.6 + 0.4*h₁)
    = tanh(0.10 + 0.06 + 0.4*0.08) = tanh(0.10 + 0.06 + 0.032) = tanh(0.192) ≈ 0.19

t=3 (word = “ate”):

x₃ = [0.7, 0.9]
h₃ = tanh(0.5*0.7 + 0.1*0.9 + 0.4*0.19)
    = tanh(0.35 + 0.09 + 0.076) = tanh(0.516) ≈ 0.475

✅ Final encoder hidden state = context vector = h₃ = 0.475

⸻

🧠 Step 4: Decoder LSTM (predict Spanish)

Target Input: <START> el gato → [0, 1, 2]
We use same weight set for simplicity.

Embedding (Spanish):

E_spa = {
  0: [0.0, 0.0],   # <START>
  1: [0.3, 0.4],   # el
  2: [0.2, 0.5],   # gato
  3: [0.6, 0.1]    # comió
}

Start with:
	•	Initial hidden state = encoder output = h₀ = 0.475

t=1 (input = <START> → [0.0, 0.0]):

h₁ = tanh(0.5*0.0 + 0.1*0.0 + 0.4*0.475) = tanh(0.0 + 0.0 + 0.19) = tanh(0.19) ≈ 0.188

t=2 (input = el → [0.3, 0.4]):

h₂ = tanh(0.5*0.3 + 0.1*0.4 + 0.4*0.188)
    = tanh(0.15 + 0.04 + 0.0752) = tanh(0.2652) ≈ 0.259

t=3 (input = gato → [0.2, 0.5]):

h₃ = tanh(0.5*0.2 + 0.1*0.5 + 0.4*0.259)
    = tanh(0.10 + 0.05 + 0.104) = tanh(0.254) ≈ 0.248


⸻

🧮 Step 5: Final Dense + Softmax

Let’s assume we have a simple output weight:

W = [0.9, 0.3, 0.6, 0.2, 0.1, 0.05]  # For 6 Spanish vocab tokens

Predicted logits at t=3:

z = h₃ × W = 0.248 × W = [0.223, 0.074, 0.149, 0.050, 0.025, 0.012]

Apply softmax (approximate):

softmax(z) ≈ probability distribution
→ highest at index 3 = "comió"

✅ So, predicted next word = "comió"

